---
import BaseLayout from '../../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout title="About" description="About the author behind this Astro Keel site.">
  <section class="page-head section">
    <p class="eyebrow">About Me</p>
    <h1>I'm Trooper</h1>
    <p class="lead">
      Currently starting my freshmen year of college. Interested in robotics, unmanned aerial systems, and mechatronics.
      In my free time I mountain bike, hangout with friends, and do some photography.
    </p>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">History</p>
      <h2>From Curiosity to Engineering</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        I would say it all started when my parents got me LEGOs. I loved building things out of them.
        I'd often build the set, then take it apart or add to it.
        Even now, I only have a few completed sets with bins of LEGOs waiting to be turned into something cool.
        Soon after, I got a snap circuits kit. I would make every project it had in the book.
        From flashing lights, to an AM radio transmitter. I didn't want to stop building, I was hooked.
      </p>
      <a class="button" href="/blog/engineering-life-story/">Read more</a>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section" aria-label="Experience summary">
    <div class="about-ledger">
      <article>
        <span>01</span>
        <h3>Why I Like Robotics</h3>
        <p>I like making things, but when they exist only in a computer I feel like they aren't real.
          So bringing the code and model into a physical object I can touch is what makes it perfect for me.</p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>02</span>
        <h3>What else I do</h3>
        <p>In my free time I enjoy spending time outdoors.
          I competed in mountain bike races all through out high school and hope to continue this sport well into my future.
          I also enjoy photography and trying to capture scenic areas.
        </p>
      </article>
      <article>
        <span>03</span>
        <h3>Contact</h3>
        <p>Email: trooperg_public_contact@pm.me</p>
        <p>This email is checked regularly and I should respond within a day or so.
          Don't spam it or use it for any other purposes besides messaging me, I can easily disable it if needed.
        </p>
      </article>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section class="section prose-grid about-closing">
    <div>
      <p class="eyebrow">Achievements</p>
      <h2>Driven by Excellence</h2>
    </div>
    <div class="prose-stack">
      <p>
        Listed below are awards and certifications I've earned in order of when I received them (newest first):
      </p>
      <p>AP Scholar Award - July 14th, 2026</p>
      <p>7th place in Computer Problem Solving at Future Business Leaders of America National Leadership Conference (FBLA) - July 2nd, 2026</p>
      <p>High School Diploma (Do I really need to state this?) - May 20th, 2026</p>
      <p>Senior Engineer of the Year - May 18th, 2026</p>
      <p>Highest Honors Graduation Stole (Graduated with &gt4.0 GPA) - May 18th, 2026</p>
      <p>SolidWorks Design Professional (CSWP) - March 31st, 2026</p>
      <p>1st place in Coding at Technology Student Association (TSA) Colorado State Competition - February 21st, 2026</p>
      <p>1st place in Drone Challenge (UAV) at TSA District Competition - December 8th, 2025</p>
      <p>2nd place in Technology Problem Solving at TSA District Competition - December 8th, 2025</p>
      <p>Received an Academic Letter in TSA - 2026</p>
      <p>Received an Academic Letter in FBLA - 2026</p>
